      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. this is good. could you maybe make it sound a little less robotic though? like, can we make it sound more like we're a tight-knit group and that it was a really tough decision for us? just something that feels a bit more \"human\" and warm without being unprofessional.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Let me try to infuse a bit more warmth into the template. You can say, \"We were blown away by the last candidate's skills, but ultimately, we decided to go with someone whose experience was a better fit for our team's needs, kind of like how a skilled tinkerer might choose to work with a specific type of metal in their craft - it's all about finding the right fit.\"\n\nHere's a revised template:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Developer position at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your skills and experience, and we're grateful for the time you took to interview with us. Your passion for coding and your enthusiasm for our company culture really resonated with us.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we've decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience align more closely with our current project requirements. It was an incredibly tough decision, as we were all blown away by your potential and the impact you could have made on our team. However, we believe that this decision will ultimately benefit our project in the long run.\n\nPlease know that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as a developer. We",
